    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title">GRADING CRITERIA:</h2>
    <div class="text-block">
        <p>Your final course grade will be assigned on a 1000-point scale as follows:</p>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <td style="width: 50%;">925+ points = A</td>
                <td style="width: 25%;">825 – 924 points = B</td>
                <td style="width: 25%;">725 – 824 points = C</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>625 – 724 points = D</td>
                <td>&lt;625 points = F</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title">YOUR FINAL GRADE WILL RESULT FROM POINTS YOU EARN ON:</h2>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th style="width: 5%;"></th>
                <th style="width: 50%;">Assignment</th>
                <th style="width: 20%;">Points Possible</th>
                <th style="width: 25%;">Total Points</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>A.)</td>
                <td>Orientation Quiz</td>
                <td>10 pts</td>
                <td>Total 10 pts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>B.)</td>
                <td>Chapter Quizzes (9 of 10)</td>
                <td>20 pts each</td>
                <td>Total 180 pts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td></td>
                <td>You will have two (2) attempts and twenty-five (25) minutes to complete each quiz. If taken, the result of the second attempt, even if lower than the first, will be recorded. The lowest one quiz grade is dropped.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>C.)</td>
                <td>Discussion Board (13)</td>
                <td>20 pts each</td>
                <td>Total 260 pts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td></td>
                <td>A minimum of three (3) posts are required within each discussion board forum. Initial posts are worth up to 15 points each. You must also reply to at least two others. Each reply post is worth up to 2.5 points.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>D.)</td>
                <td>Writing Exercise (10 of 11)</td>
                <td>25 pts each</td>
                <td>Total 250 pts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td></td>
                <td>Similar to the discussion board forums, prompts for this assignment will be provided. Your responses, however, will not be shared with or responded to by your peers. The lowest one writing exercise grade is dropped.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>E.)</td>
                <td>Film Analysis Paper</td>
                <td>100 pts</td>
                <td>Total 100 pts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td></td>
                <td>Instructions will be found under the FILM ANALYSIS tab after October 30th.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>F.)</td>
                <td>Visual Essay</td>
                <td>100 pts</td>
                <td>Total 100 pts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td></td>
                <td>Instructions will be found under the VISUAL ESSAY tab after October 30th.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>G.)</td>
                <td>Final Exam</td>
                <td>100 pts</td>
                <td>Total 100 pts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td></td>
                <td>The comprehensive final exam will consist of fifty (50) multiple-choice and true/false questions each. You will have two (2) attempts and sixty (60) minutes to complete the exam. The result of the second attempt, even if lower than the first, will be recorded.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
        <p style="font-weight: bold;">**Your final grade is based on points earned, not a percentage**</p>
        <p style="font-weight: bold;">**Lowest grades are dropped from the beginning, not at the end, of the course**</p>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">MAKE-UP and/or LATE WORK & EXTRA CREDIT</h3>
    <div class="text-block">
        <p>Late work will not be graded and make up work is not allowed.</p>
        <p>No additional opportunities for extra credit will be offered.</p>
    </div>
</div>

